name: Explicit engine-option cleanup preserves global choices through Scan, Review and restart
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN SEMGREP_AGENT_TOKEN
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_option_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 35 context:build indexed | prepared-context
submit: use threat-model
submit: options threat-model:import
submit: set path .kuzushi/manual-context.json
submit: set activate false
submit: set label Owned manual policy context
submit: run threat-model:import
require-live-snap: 35 threat-model:import saved | imported-context
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 SYSTEM SUMMARY | map-result
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Map ✓ | accepted-map
submit: use sast
submit: options sast:scan
submit: setg taskMode manual
submit: setg tasks semgrep
paste-file: @ART/old-rule-setting.txt
keys: Enter
submit: setg semgrepTimeoutMs 60000
submit: setg semgrepJobs 1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_option_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART globals
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | original-study
keys: Home Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CHOOSE DISCOVERY ENGINES | original-engines
expect: [x] semgrep
keys: Space Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Space
require-live-snap: 20 c clear unused | inactive-options
expect: [x] license-scan
expect: semgrepConfig
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Selection needs attention | invalid-apply-retained
expect: No changes applied
ask: Does switching engines explain the retained settings, keep the invalid choice editable, and offer explicit cleanup without changing global choices or starting work?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 15 c clear unused | cleanup-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 15 c clear unused | cleanup-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 15 c clear unused | cleanup-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 15 c clear unused | cleanup-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 c clear unused | cleanup-40x12
keys: NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage
require-live-snap: 15 guarantee. | cleanup-detail-tail
ask: Are cleanup, apply and cancel visible at every size, with the complete explanation reachable at 40 columns?
resize: 120x36
keys: c
require-live-snap: 20 Cleared semgrepConfig | cleared-local-draft
expect-not: c clear unused
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 Discovery engines  current settings | canceled-cleanup
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_option_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART cancelled
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 CHOOSE DISCOVERY ENGINES | restored-original-options
expect: [x] semgrep
keys: Space Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Space
require-live-snap: 20 c clear unused | restored-inactive-options
keys: c a
require-live-snap: 20 Engine choices updated | applied-cleanup
expect: Discovery engines  license-scan
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_option_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART applied
ask: Does Cancel preserve the original study, while explicit clear and apply retain source/context, global settings and spending and require a new plan?
keys: Home Down Down Down Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Total calls | total-calls
keys: C-a
type: 1
keys: Enter Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Protected review | protected-review
keys: C-a
type: 1
keys: Enter L
require-live-snap: 35 Draft ready | clean-finite-plan
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_option_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART draft
keys: L Home
require-live-snap: 25 REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE | approval
expect: 3 fixed jobs
expect: Total provider calls: 1
expect: Protected review calls: 1
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 y approve | full-approval-terms
keys: y
require-live-snap: 25 Approval saved | approved-study
keys: L
require-live-snap: 25 3 planned | fixed-jobs
keys: L
require-live-snap: 25 dispatcher pid | launched
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_option_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART completed
keys: r
require-live-snap: 25 3 completed | completed-study
submit: workbench
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Scan | scan-result
nav-mode:
keys: n
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Review | accepted-scan
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Package manifest does not declare a license | finding
expect: signal-only
submit: decision deferred Owned package policy needs an owner decision
require-live-snap: 25 Owned package policy needs an owner decision | deferred
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Enter export | report
keys: Down Down Down
require-live-snap: 25 format json (4/6) | json-format
require-live-snap: 25 Enter export/retry | export-ready
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 json · 1 finding(s) | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_option_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
ask: Does the revised plan execute exactly three local passes, consolidate one signal-only finding, preserve its human decision, and export without consuming protected provider capacity?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/resume-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 3 completed | recovered-jobs
nav-mode:
keys: a Home Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 CHOOSE DISCOVERY ENGINES | recovered-local-choices
expect: [x] license-scan
expect-not: c clear unused
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Engine choices retained | exact-plan-retained
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Owned package policy needs an owner decision | recovered-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_option_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain the clean local plan and decision while the original global scanner settings remain saved and no extra work starts?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
